{"updated_at": {"date": {"d": "10", "m": "10", "Y": "2026"}, "time": {"H": "14", "M": "03", "S": "42"}}, "news": [{"title": "Telangana speeds up GO 59 land regularisation, collectors told to clear backlog", "para": "The Telangana government is urging district collectors to swiftly handle the backlog of land regularisation applications. Revenue Minister Ponguleti Srinivas Reddy highlighted the necessity of meticulous verification prior to any approvals. This strategic initiative seeks to alleviate the persistent difficulties encountered by applicants dealing with encroached government lands.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/industry/telangana-speeds-up-go-59-land-regularisation-collectors-told-to-clear-backlog/134847385?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-71872/134847385.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "industry"}, {"title": "NGT directs Chennai civic body to ensure strict adherence by builders to construction waste rules", "para": "The National Green Tribunal directed the Greater Chennai Corporation to maintain uninterrupted processing of construction waste. It was noted that facilities for this purpose stopped functioning in early 2024, highlighting an essential need for alternative solutions. The tribunal mandated that compliance with waste management guidelines must be integral to building-plan approvals.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/regulatory/ngt-directs-chennai-civic-body-to-ensure-strict-adherence-by-builders-to-construction-waste-rules/134847361?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-151915/134847361.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "regulatory"}, {"title": "Gurugram: DTCP seals five buildings in Sushant Lok-1 for commercial use of residential premises", "para": "In Sushant Lok-1, the Department of Town and Country Planning embarked on a significant operation aimed at enforcing local regulations. During the initiative, five buildings were sealed due to their unauthorized commercial activities within residential areas. This included two paying guest accommodations and a guest house, underscoring a continuous commitment to curbing such breaches. District town planner Amit Madholia highlighted the ongoing nature of these enforcement actions.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/residential/gurugram-dtcp-seals-five-buildings-in-sushant-lok-1-for-commercial-use-of-residential-premises/134847207?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-119660/134847207.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "residential"}]}